- The overall design of the Sprint Review presentation was very good and got complimented a lot 
- We had a good discussion about acceptance criteria and how we should validate them
- The organization of issues and PRs is improving, although there is still room for improvement
- Communication is improving in some areas, but we still have issues with responsiveness and coordination

## 3. What did not

- There was a lack of communication on Discord, with messages sometimes going unanswered.
- PRs were not always reviewed within a reasonable amount of time, leaving people waiting before they could continue their work.
- It was not always clear who was working on which tasks.
- Some group members felt excluded from contributing because they were unsure what work was available or already being handled by other people
- The lack of coordination sometimes resulted in people being unable to progress with their tasks.
- Issues and PRs are still somewhat disorganized, making it harder to follow the progress of the work.

## 4. Where we lost time

- Some PRs were left waiting for reviews for several days.
- This delayed the process of receiving feedback, making corrections and completing the work.
- Unanswered Discord messages caused unnecessary waiting and uncertainty.
- Time was lost because it was unclear who was responsible for certain tasks and what others were currently working on.
- Some group members had difficulty finding work they could contribute to because the distribution of tasks was not sufficiently visible.

## 5. Cross-team

- We need better communication about what each team is currently working on.
- The distribution of PBIs and responsibilities should be clearer to avoid confusion and duplicated work
- External reviewers can provide a less biased perspective on the solution
- We need clearer expectations for PR reviews, including how quickly reviews should be handled and what to do when a reviewer is unavailable. 
- If a PR is not getting any response quick enough, they should ping the relevant group in the Discord
- Reviewers should explicitly communicate when they cannot review something immediately.
- The Integration Team should help identify dependencies and ensure relevant information is shared between teams.
- everyone should at minimum react to messages in the discord to show that they have seen it, even if they are not responding to it
- instead of assuming a message is not for you and that someone else will PROBABLY answer, assume that you should just answer if you are able to

## 6. One improvement for next sprint

**Improvement:** Improve communication and coordination of tasks and PR reviews.

We need to make it clearer who is working on what, who is responsible for reviewing PRs, and when reviews can be expected. If someone cannot review a PR or respond to a question, this should be communicated so that others are not left waiting without knowing when they can continue.

**Owner:** {Name}

**How we will know:**

- Tasks and responsibilities are visible to the group.
- PRs receive reviews within an agreed timeframe, or delays are communicated.
- Group members know what work is available and who is currently working on what.
- Fewer tasks are delayed because of unanswered messages or pending reviews.

